WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.960
A baby at a font.

2
00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.180
Water is poured over the head three times.

3
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.490
Across town, another church baptises only
people old enough to say for themselves

4
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.930
that they believe.

5
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.460
Both use water.

6
00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.730
Both use the same words:
in the name of the Father,

7
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.670
and of the Son, and of the Holy Spirit.

8
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.390
So why do some Christians baptise babies,

9
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:25.870
while others wait until people
can choose for themselves?

10
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.470
In this mission, you'll see why
those words name the Father,

11
00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.770
the Son and the Holy Spirit.

12
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.150
Then you'll follow a baby's
baptism, step by step,

13
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.820
and find out what each sign means.

14
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:42.760
Your mission: find out why Christians
disagree about who should be baptised.
